## Why it exists

Under host pressure the test suite produced a **different 2–4 failures on every run**, with whole
test files failing to collect and **no assertion** — the signature of worker timeouts, not broken
code. A saturated host makes the suite signal worthless.

## Server hygiene

- **Turbopack is broken in this worktree** (`next dev --turbopack` → "Next.js package not found").
  Use `npx next start --port 3111` against a production build. `next dev` overwrites `.next`.
- Check `lsof -ti :3111` first: reuse a running server, or start one and clean it up with
  `lsof -ti :3111 | xargs kill -9`. **Never kill a process you did not start.**
- Playwright's `webServer` config would start the broken Turbopack server, so start
  `next start` on 3111 yourself and Playwright will reuse it.

## Host health gate (run before any suite)

```
uptime                                   # load1 < 40
vm_stat | grep -E 'Pages (free|inactive)'   # available = free+inactive+spec+purgeable > 1.5 GiB
```

If the gate fails, **delay** and report it. A suite result obtained under load is discarded,
not trusted.
